big-fella: the Standard Dolby Vision RGB8 tunnel on amdgpu DC

The DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB connector property of yblod's i915 patches
(linux-9900 to 9903), with the same semantics, on native HDMI connectors of
DCN 1.0 to 3.6 (amdgpu.enable_dv_lab, default on), so kwin-big-fella and
dv-engine-vk work unchanged on AMD integrated graphics:

- the property: atomic bool per HDMI-A connector; 1 needs HDMI-A and the
  option; back to 0 when the connector loses its CRTC; a change is a full
  modeset (mode_changed, and DC sees a changed stream: dc_is_timing_changed);
- the link policy: i915's own intel_dv_lab_validate() and dvbridge_parse_edid()
  (included from i915/display, MIT, inline), with DC's stream as input: native
  TMDS HDMI, a Standard DV sink, RGB 8 bpc, full range, no HDR metadata,
  Colorspace Default, max bpc 8, progressive 1080p/2160p at 24/25/30/50/60 with
  a CTA VIC, 2160p above 30 Hz only if the sink says so. Run in
  dm_update_crtc_state() only (not mode_valid, which uses the connector's
  current state and would prune the mode list while the tunnel is engaged);
- the stream: DC's own AVI InfoFrame as RGB, no colorimetry, full range
  (COLOR_SPACE_SRGB, qs_bit), CTA VIC; the Dolby VSIF (or, for v0/v1 sinks,
  the HDMI-1.4b VSIF with its Dolby Vision bit and HDMI VIC, as i915) in the
  vendor slot; no HF-VSIF/VTEM; dither and truncation off (FMT); FreeSync's
  packet off;
- the scanout policy, at the end of amdgpu_dm_atomic_check() for every CRTC
  driving a tunnel stream: no CRTC or plane colour processing (CTM, degamma,
  gamma, AMD plane LUTs/TFs, COLOR_PIPELINE), no VRR or async flips, no DSC,
  no scaling or borders, the primary plane alone on the CRTC with an
  unscaled, unrotated, opaque XRGB8888 buffer of the mode's size;
- diagnostics: i915's rate-limited "DVBridge: link rejected" and "DVBridge:
  scanout rejected ... reasons=0x..." messages; the engaged stream's packets
  with drm.debug=0x4.

Not ported: QMS (linux-9910/9911; a refresh change is a modeset on amdgpu),
the SPD source type (linux-9912; amdgpu sends no SPD InfoFrame of its own),
DVBRIDGE_HDR10_DEEP_COLOR (linux-9904).

DC hook points adapted from CroqueMr's CB1 (github.com/CroqueMr/libreelec-x86-DV,
projects/Generic/patches/linux/linux-9920-amd-dcn-native-dv.patch and
linux-9921-amd-dv-diagnostic-and-vrr-guards.patch, MIT). Applies after
linux-9900 to linux-9912. See big-fella's docs/dv-amd.md.

